# Backend

Thin Express BFF. Consumer of scoring data — never compute a score.

- Routes live on the main Agricultural Credit Platform API (`backend/`, port 3000): `GET /api/readiness/:lookup` (10/min/IP), `POST .../actions/:id/complete`, `POST .../loan-application` (OTP required), `POST /api/otp/request`, `GET /api/admin/flagged-accounts`
- Scoring stays in `CreditEngineService` (300–850). Readiness maps that to the 0–100 farmer display scale — do not invent a second algorithm
- Outbound shaping through `my-readiness/backend/src/clients/corePlatform.js` (in-process `ReadinessService`, else demo mocks)
- Localize raw keys into the display-ready payload in `my-readiness/backend/src/lib/localize.js`
- Dynamic farmer text (why, action how/impact, climate) may pass through Featherless when `FEATHERLESS_API_KEY` is set; static UI stays in i18n files
- Env: Firebase client SDK (`FIREBASE_API_KEY` + `FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID`, optional Auth email/password), Africa's Talking (`AT_USERNAME`, `AT_API_KEY`, `AT_CALLBACK_SECRET`), `FEATHERLESS_API_KEY`, `FEATHERLESS_MODEL`, `DEFAULT_LOCALE`, `PORT`
- USSD lives on the core API: `POST /api/ussd` (Africa's Talking callback). Same ReadinessService as the PWA — do not score inside the USSD handler
- Loan amount is always server-derived from eligibility — never accept amount from the client
- OTP only wraps loan submit; score/improve stay public
